{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And abashed.</b> The sense concerns the moon and the sun, for they rule, and behold the kings of the earth shall be ashamed; also the sun shall be darkened and the moon — then you will see the kingdom of HaShem on Mount Zion, then there will be glory for those who cleave to HaShem. And some say the sense concerns worshippers of the luminaries, and it does not accord with the sense of the pericope."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:01.082877635Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}